      "message": "(Posting on the most related CL, probably worth its own patch)\n\nNote that this currently prevents the VMM from registering for handling the HVC i.e.\n```\nioctl(KVM_SET_DEVICE_ATTR, kvm_device_attr {\n    KVM_ARM_VM_SMCCC_CTRL,\n    KVM_ARM_VM_SMCCC_FILTER,\n    kvm_smccc_filter {\n        base,\n        nr_functions,\n        KVM_SMCCC_FILTER_FWD_TO_USER,\n    }\n})\n```\nMy current one-line hack to work around it:\n```\ndiff --git a/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_pkvm.h b/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_pkvm.h\nindex 488000c486c6..8f62e6be400b 100644\n--- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_pkvm.h\n+++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_pkvm.h\n@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ static inline bool kvm_pkvm_ext_allowed(struct kvm *kvm, long ext)\n        case KVM_CAP_ARM_PTRAUTH_ADDRESS:\n        case KVM_CAP_ARM_PTRAUTH_GENERIC:\n        case KVM_CAP_ARM_PROTECTED_VM:\n+       case KVM_CAP_DEVICE_CTRL:\n                return true;\n        case KVM_CAP_ARM_MTE:\n                return false;\n```",
